Let the speed of the swimmer be x m/s in and the current is y m/s respectively
The swimmer started from P and swam 360 seconds to R against the current, then return to Q swimming for 360 seconds.
PR = 360[x – y] ....{1}
QR = 360[x + y] ....{2}
PQ = QR – PR
{From 1 and 2}
⇒ 120 = 360[x + y - x + y]
⇒ y = <img src="https://www.thepunditsofficial.in/admin/uploads/questions/q_698809de31be21.41116748.gif"> m/s
The speed of the current = <img src="https://www.thepunditsofficial.in/admin/uploads/questions/q_698809de4a2fa6.77761150.gif"> m/s = <img src="https://www.thepunditsofficial.in/admin/uploads/questions/q_698809de71b471.49077771.gif"> × <img src="https://www.thepunditsofficial.in/admin/uploads/questions/q_698809de926840.81267576.gif"> = 0.6 km/hr

